commons docs.fence

----
A doc-block opened with four dashes closes only on four, so it can hold a
`---` line, such as a Markdown rule:

---

and a Bynk example that carries its own doc-block:

```bynk
---
A doc-block inside a doc example.
---
fn example() -> Int { 1 }
```
----
fn answer() -> Int { 42 }

---
A plain three-dash doc-block, as before.
---
fn double(n: Int) -> Int { n * 2 }
